<InfoPage title="Editorial Policy" kicker="How we publish" description="Our standards for original Musebox AI video comparisons, sources, updates, consent boundaries, and corrections."><h2>Useful before optimized</h2><p>Each page must help a reader make a concrete production or safety decision. Keywords belong in descriptive titles, headings, and natural explanations—not repeated sentences or hidden blocks.</p><h2>Primary sources</h2><p>Product claims link to official pages when available. Broader safety principles rely on recognized primary guidance. Sources appear in each article so readers and generative search systems can verify context.</p><h2>Clear boundaries</h2><p>Coverage is for adults and emphasizes licensed source media, explicit consent, privacy, disclosure, cost visibility, deletion, and harm prevention. We do not request source images or generated intimate media for editorial review.</p><h2>Corrections</h2><p>Material changes update the visible revision date. Correction requests should identify the page, disputed text, and a direct source supporting the change.</p></InfoPage>
